3. COMMERCIAL GRANT

A completed, non-refunded purchase from the Licensor or an authorized seller grants
the identified purchaser a non-exclusive right to use and privately modify the
Software within the purchased scope. A sole proprietor or legal entity is one
licensee. Parent companies, subsidiaries and unrelated businesses are separate
licensees unless expressly included by a written agreement.

Single Project covers one commercial application/product, including SaaS, and its
development, staging, production and disaster-recovery deployments. Users, tenants,
workspaces and multiple instances of that same product do not create new projects.

Unlimited covers unlimited own applications and integrated applications developed
for clients by one licensee. Authorized employees and contractors may work within
that licensee's scope. It does not permit sharing the purchaser's license key or
package credentials between unrelated businesses or agencies.

Business has the same project scope as Unlimited and includes twelve months of
priority product support as described in section 5. All paid plans include the
same Software features; plan differences concern usage scope and support.

A covered client application may be delivered with the Software as an integrated
part, and the client may continue operating that covered application. This does
not give the client or a subsequent maintainer rights to use the Software in other
projects or share the purchaser's credentials. Access to future package updates
requires a valid entitlement held by an authorized licensee.

4. VERSIONS, UPDATES AND CONTINUED USE

Each standard commercial purchase includes twelve months of Software updates from
the purchase date. You may keep using, reinstalling and deploying versions released
within that entitlement period indefinitely within your purchased project scope,
subject to this agreement. Expiry of updates alone does not terminate those rights.
Later releases require a new or renewed update entitlement. Lifetime updates,
automatic renewal and subscription charges are not included. Renewal or upgrade
terms, if offered, must be stated separately before purchase.

5. SUPPORT AND EXTERNAL SERVICES

Business includes twelve months of priority handling for product-specific technical
support requests from purchase. Requests are prioritized over the standard support
